1. Kf5 { White approaches from the side. } 1... Rb6 { Black keeps the sixth-rank barrier while avoiding the file occupied by White’s rook. } 2. e5 { White advances the pawn. } 2... Rh6 { Black continues to deny the sixth rank. } 3. e6 { The pawn reaches the sixth rank, changing the defensive task. } 3... Rh1 { Black goes behind the attacking king to prepare checks. } 4. Kf6 { White tries to improve the king. } 4... Rh6+ { Black checks from the side; the pawn no longer supplies shelter behind the king. } *

